{"type":"message","id":"c6f077ca","parentId":"27986592","timestamp":"2026-03-17T16:52:05.128Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] That makes a **urinary/kidney source more concerning**, especially with your history. Blood in the urine plus burning can fit **urinary tract irritation/infection**, but it can also occur with **stones, bleeding, or other urinary tract/kidney problems**, so it meaningfully raises concern beyond simple back strain.\n\nPlease answer the **remaining 3 questions**:\n\n3. Any **fever, chills, nausea/vomiting, unintentional weight loss, or night sweats**?  \n4. Are you currently still taking **sunitinib**, and when did the exhaustion start in relation to that treatment?  \n5. Any **new leg weakness, numbness, tingling, or loss of bowel/bladder control**?","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b6dba701581cd2e0169b986b202508191a569a740c6496823\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":488,"output":160,"cacheRead":35584,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":36232,"cost":{"input":0.0012200000000000002,"output":0.0024000000000000002,"cacheRead":0.008896,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.012516}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773766320883}}
