{"type":"message","id":"838c8c1d","parentId":"51ef0828","timestamp":"2026-03-17T16:53:22.062Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Considering urgent health concerns**\n\nI need to address the full output regarding the user’s health issues like numbness, blood problems, weight loss, and medical history. It seems urgent, so I might suggest using a tool related to kidney evaluations, if that fits. Additionally, I should recommend that the user uploads their CT scan for further analysis. I want to make sure I’m considering the right factors and providing helpful guidance for their situation!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0b6dba701581cd2e0169b986e8eeb0819180f4fb9f577aefa0\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpuYbrqJ4xZ5DNhK8P0MA513qyY_VlmBW6WrS5J9ueXRwdZPERS_oCHBZVCACdNR89T4odHonHoBS4hN6e_pS87B9E0L-WfzP0Vj9LPx6F3qWue0GQfvAL9zCpWXXZVEicWo6ZBHEnKlzh8Ixv5zNbLAZP9kHPXDl1gurXdqKgDaQ5rgIdk-a6jIZamCtUEJC3EakPEfHUUpUS24Ail4DhiEo7GcZ25vL1bBkGhGpgg4YuGGR5ue8mAPIrugmnJeGdsCFNhOlB0as2LSRV90emYt8u-bI6P0bqbymkZiohavpAtmHqkexpAiU0eZ7UOyl73170_GXIlrgUuNIEQYOjbihj7lzFd7jZU7ATuiGfhX8o3cJDBoKJTm3dEIHtamRpABbYCT54ilXn2GZezCS4o1u9SD9jsjN3mBEEA8dJrt2aDEqHaGm7PRvMWqAsehuFpoQ3EuaaBPt7mPf7svy5iWAr1yXGWZc74UnJ-uitiyh1E7W3d7ZPumSRMZ-mf2OJBsV5dmCiT9EuovJ873sGoXVD12OPkXOsq1ivTsczOV3drwqyyWPMqi9UtQmKvGrLqe69KAkZ-y9g64PJ2K8cXbRcaUNWgrNLsas6bEVtVGPzC8ZWHtpFOOt9y17TIeYVeNFDL_1OMMZh38HgkSotuTfmf6Bt70g6D_mfslK66YARpoCnyTFLuzUWvqLBTRxo8W30qwi3TX_4qKq5xfXDANRzI-fnnIX5KjUk3oyyN8KkX7TVPpSCtHews8Tm6M6tWXeGduAp4RABSTvfoKTJjPtGJSCH-D8F2t8kFw0MbKJMOHjctelpYpzvVzdPeZBs8tqVXijKfCn_OzqUWaKaYLb6ZHp0MUwWGJFvO3i0hptfRlxEaWjioCxxI70FrEhK6uKPlrrZzf80oi6nyQJ9s5ZXvryd8AFZ2iXHvIWW0h18FSI4r9XMbgSn8N6OCQMJe1CzmRnwg87zb9UM2uK3F_CzIZ9f1kQz6_4BP8OWNFh43HxQNwgzgEHcQ37PDnanEDfmoYnbr5ELreuSunnLEbhzoQ==\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Considering urgent health concerns**\\n\\nI need to address the full output regarding the user’s health issues like numbness, blood problems, weight loss, and medical history. It seems urgent, so I might suggest using a tool related to kidney evaluations, if that fits. Additionally, I should recommend that the user uploads their CT scan for further analysis. I want to make sure I’m considering the right factors and providing helpful guidance for their situation!\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] ### Clinical picture\n- You’ve described **months of worsening dull pain in the right low back near the spine**, along with **significant exhaustion**.\n- You also reported **blood in the urine**, **burning with urination**, **unintentional weight loss**, and **some leg numbness**.\n- From your record, there is major relevant history of **right clear cell renal cell carcinoma**, **post-nephrectomy follow-up**, **chronic kidney disease / reduced kidney function**, prior **hematuria**, and family/genomic kidney cancer risk.\n- Taken together, this is **more concerning than routine back pain**.\n\n### Most likely possibilities\n1. **Kidney / urinary tract problem that needs prompt medical reassessment**\n   - Blood in the urine, burning, fatigue, and your prior kidney cancer history make this a leading concern.\n   - This could reflect **recurrence/progression, another renal/urologic lesion, bleeding, obstruction, infection, or stone disease**.\n2. **Spine or nerve-related process**\n   - Low back pain near the spine with **leg numbness** can fit **lumbar nerve irritation/compression**.\n   - In your setting, this cannot be assumed to be benign without evaluation.\n3. **Infection or inflammatory urinary issue**\n   - Burning plus hematuria could fit a **UTI** or related urinary tract irritation, though the chronic worsening and weight loss make me less reassured by infection alone.\n4. **CKD- or anemia-related fatigue**\n   - Your prior records show reduced kidney function, and fatigue may be partly worsened by **CKD, anemia, or systemic illness**.\n\n### Confidence / uncertainty note\n- I’m **fairly concerned** that this needs **prompt in-person assessment**.\n- I cannot determine here whether the main driver is **urologic/kidney**, **spinal/neurologic**, or a combination.\n- The most important uncertainty is whether the **leg numbness** reflects a simple radicular problem or something more urgent, and whether the urinary findings reflect **infection vs bleeding vs recurrence/progression**.\n\n### Red flags / urgent concerns\n- **Blood in the urine + weight loss + fatigue + cancer history** are red flags.\n- **Leg numbness** adds concern for a **neurologic/spinal complication**, especially if it is worsening.\n- You should seek **urgent medical evaluation today / as soon as possible**, ideally through your **oncology/urology team or urgent care / emergency assessment**, especially if any of these are present now:\n  - worsening numbness or weakness\n  - trouble walking\n  - loss of bladder or bowel control\n  - severe or rapidly worsening pain\n  - fever/chills\n  - vomiting\n  - reduced urine output\n  - heavy / visible ongoing bleeding in urine\n\n### Recommended next questions\n- You’ve answered the key questions I needed.\n\n### Suggested tool/skill use\n- Because this is kidney-focused and your history includes **right renal cell carcinoma**, you could use the **specialized kidney cancer detection pipeline** **if you have a recent CT image scan to upload**.\n- If you run that tool, I can help interpret the result carefully as a **preliminary signal, not a diagnosis**.\n- After a tool run, I’d also suggest using the **LLM Distillation** tool to turn the findings and your symptom history into a clearer patient-facing summary.\n\n### Recommended next step\n- Given everything you’ve shared, I would **not wait passively on this**. Please arrange **prompt in-person evaluation today**, especially because of the **hematuria, weight loss, and leg numbness**.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0b6dba701581cd2e0169b986eb21bc8191a872500daaa430cb\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":228,"output":801,"cacheRead":36608,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":37637,"cost":{"input":0.0005700000000000001,"output":0.012015,"cacheRead":0.009152,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.021737}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773766373595}}
{"type":"message","id":"1937e6db","parentId":"838c8c1d","timestamp":"2026-03-17T16:53:42.821Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[media attached: /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/kidney_test2---55fe09ea-9865-48be-a13c-b75cf1196d84.jpg (image/jpeg) | /home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/kidney_test2---55fe09ea-9865-48be-a13c-b75cf1196d84.jpg]\nTo send an image back, prefer the message tool (media/path/filePath). If you must inline, use MEDIA:https://example.com/image.jpg (spaces ok, quote if needed) or a safe relative path like MEDIA:./image.jpg. Avoid absolute paths (MEDIA:/...) and ~ paths — they are blocked for security. Keep caption in the text body.\nConversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"221\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"495506013\",\n  \"sender\": \"Matteo Cicalese\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Tue 2026-03-17 16:53 UTC\"\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"Matteo Cicalese (495506013)\",\n  \"id\": \"495506013\",\n  \"name\": \"Matteo Cicalese\",\n  \"username\": \"CicaMatt\"\n}\n```\n\nOkay, can you please run a kidney analysis on my CT scan?"},{"type":"image","data":"","mimeType":"image/jpeg"}],"timestamp":1773766422818}}
